{
  "status": "Focused live producer, compact frozen-provider controls and settlement visibility verified in both modes; complete restart/early reservation/application contracts remain unfinished",
  "source_sha256": "069bb71d6765d7c6ddf3db2a1bc5f7d3c0f8890456eb79925677c2b32f8a4e15",
  "shared_entry": "Host::start_owned_command selects a journal primitive, then one Journal::execute producer uses the same slot admission, lease-owned executor, original invocation and backend mutation policy in both modes.",
  "adapters": [
    "BackendClient service callbacks",
    "PairedCommandJournal command-purpose callbacks"
  ],
  "implemented": [
    "Reacquire the original private recovery permit under the complete physical folder lease, refresh original identity after queued waits and persist a native intent before command-worker admission.",
    "Schema4 anchored native command slots physically reserve a complete bounded result and ownership metadata before any RPC. Prepared, Admitted, Dispatched and Finished transitions never infer permission to replay from a reconnect.",
    "Persist the single dispatch boundary immediately before the mutating RPC. Keep the original service and lease through cleanup, native outcome publication, backend Finish/Settle and native owner retirement.",
    "Publish original command outcomes independently of the browser. Successful cleanup/settlement retires the compound owner and preserves the warm language server. Duplicate starts join the same native result.",
    "A definitely unadmitted native intent can publish a no-dispatch rejection without a new manual grant. No command RPC is sent; the separate manual acknowledgement precedes background settlement.",
    "Original retained physical leases may publish private uncertainty after pathname loss or quarantine, while current workspace mutation, redispatch and retirement remain denied.",
    "A changed original execution folder after RPC becomes uncertainty and stops the original service. Missing positive cleanup never restores write access.",
    "Core CommandOperation invocation validation is shared by the action client and backend: Status/Stop can inspect recorded outcome phases without fresh dispatch authority; Start remains forbidden after a recorded outcome.",
    "Shared backend command authorization returns a stored outcome for Status without contacting the original host. Stop resolves from that outcome only after positive native cleanup; Start never uses a cached result. Paired frontend context checks precede its early return.",
    "Public ActionRecovery snapshots validate immutable original invocation, result fingerprints and native settlement flags without decoding archived provider/source payloads. Legacy readable approvals gain original metadata once; unreadable records without that metadata remain pending.",
    "Public compact Finish/Acknowledge and existing full record calls share storage phase/outcome/CAS policy. Owned native results cannot be replaced; acknowledgement requires positive cleanup and retains the independent settlement fence.",
    "Recover controls from the actual original native session or receipt, without client-supplied provider configuration or folder access. Start alone requires complete approval/provider/source and fresh manual authority.",
    "The frontend recovery facade does not enumerate installed providers. Reload retains completed/acknowledged pending settlements and blocks disk saves until native settlement clears.",
    "Native command preparation is included in the standard bridge authentication inventory. Missing/invalid service or paired credentials fail before entering the preparation handler."
  ],
  "bounds": {
    "native_database_bytes": 16777216,
    "outstanding_command_slots": 32,
    "slot_bytes": 278528,
    "outcome_bytes": 262144,
    "private_reply_bytes": 65536,
    "preparation_metadata_reserve_bytes": 4096
  },
  "actual_contracts": [
    "Real retained LSP review/preparation, native file application, independent file-worker release, post-edit synchronization, native command once, backend publication/settlement, ordinary folder admission and warm-service retention in both modes.",
    "The same real producer in both modes rejects a bad native manual grant without RPC, keeps protection pending, accepts the distinct user acknowledgement and settles in a detached bounded worker.",
    "After actual producer settlement, public backend Status/Stop authorization returns the original invocation without a fresh grant; a new Start is denied.",
    "A full Unicode outcome persists without increasing the preallocated SQLite image size. Reopening preserves the original intent/result and duplicate dispatch or replacement outcome is rejected.",
    "After root replacement and lease quarantine, the actual retained original handle can persist uncertainty but cannot regain workspace writes or redispatch.",
    "Native review/admission fixtures use a persistent original test issuer and real storage CAS over service/paired HTTP primitives; no successful LSP verification is synthesized.",
    "Real backend HTTP dispatch/authorization in both modes returns Completed, Rejected and Uncertain outcomes without an installed provider, manual grant or connected host. Other-account access fails. Stop without positive cleanup still requires the host.",
    "Both-mode storage native-worker transitions keep uncertain Stop unresolved until an original worker positively upgrades cleanup. The pending settlement fence remains intact.",
    "The real both-mode native producer ignores a client-echoed forged progress result and continues enforcing original dispatch/admission, once-only RPC and persisted publication.",
    "Both-mode public storage recovery reads unreadable original provider/source and file payloads, validates outcome fingerprints/bounds and forbids another account or a new Start. Cleanup then manual acknowledgement keeps activity/deletion blocked until the original worker settles.",
    "Real backend HTTP freezes the stored approval and still returns compact authorization/recovery and acknowledgement in both modes; account isolation and no-store responses remain enforced.",
    "Actual browser cases cover completed/acknowledged settlement save blocking, five reload/recovery cases and two late-response cases across accounts and workspace ownership.",
    "A separate actual HTTP regression first reproduced unauthenticated command preparation reaching its handler, then verifies 401 for missing/invalid credentials and authenticated handler access for both service and paired transports. The older complete command-dispatch HTTP fixture is retained and still needs real backend/bootstrap state.",
    "The complete original native HTTP join/stop/Git/round-trip/cache-removal fixture now runs against real approvals, file admission, native command preparation and both callback transports in an isolated test namespace. See command-http-checks.json for admitted settlement coverage and the remaining early-stop lifecycle limitation."
  ],
